-- #1047 BYSTANDER fixture — "feature present, UNRELATED code still behaves".
--
-- AGENTS.md: for a change that adds a program-global table, the required fixture is
-- NOT "the feature works" (entry.mdk of iface_name_collision_default is that one) —
-- it is a program where the new construct is PRESENT while every asserted value
-- comes from code that does not use it.  A fixture that only exercises the feature
-- passes by construction and proves nothing about the rest of the corpus.
--
-- So: the colliding `Speak` pair (bysa/bysb + their method-less implementors) is in
-- the module graph and is REACHED — `sayA`/`sayB` are called on the `let _` line
-- below, which keeps them out of source DCE on the emit arms — but NOTHING they
-- return is asserted.  Every printed line comes from `Greet`/`Wave`, whose interface
-- AND method names are unique in the program, so exactly ONE `CImplDefault` exists
-- per method and #1047's identity narrowing must never fire: each of these must be
-- byte-for-byte what first-match returned before the fix.
--
--   glub  — `Greet`'s default, inherited cross-module by a METHOD-LESS `impl Greet
--           Fish`.  This is the `emitDefaultRKey` / eval `pickTagFallback` route,
--           the pair #1047 changed.
--   claw  — `Wave`'s OVERRIDE for Crab: the tagged path, untouched by the fix.
--   ~     — `Wave`'s default, inherited by Fish ALONGSIDE Crab's override, so the
--           method has a default AND a tagged impl at once.
--   glub  — `Greet`'s default at a SECOND inheriting type, so the per-(method, tag)
--           default define is emitted twice under two tags from one entry.
--
-- ⚠️ Every call here is DIRECT (RKey), deliberately: a CONSTRAINED forwarder would
-- route through the runtime dict dispatcher, and wasm has NO interface-default arms
-- there (#1020) — such a fixture traps on wasm and would need an
-- engine_divergence.txt row, which is not what a bystander fixture is for.  The
-- dict-routed default chain (llvm's emitDefaultDispatchChain, which this PR also
-- touches) is covered on eval+native by the sibling fixtures
-- inherited_default_dict_dispatch / attributed_impl_dispatch, already ledgered for
-- wasm under #1020.
--
-- ⚠️ This corpus is PRELUDE-FREE (diff_compiler_llvm_modules.sh passes an EMPTY
-- core), so no prelude default can be asserted here.  The prelude's own defaults —
-- where the overwhelming majority of this tree's `CImplDefault` entries live — are
-- covered by the prelude-bearing corpora instead (diff_compiler_engines' llvm/ arm,
-- test/eval_fixtures, the doctest suite).
import bysai.{DogA(..), sayA}
import bysbi.{DogB(..), sayB}
import bysother.{Greet(..), greet, Wave(..), wave}
import bysfish.{Fish(..), Crab(..)}

main : <IO> Unit
main =
  let _ = sayA DogA ++ sayB DogB
  let _ = putStrLn (greet Fish)
  let _ = putStrLn (wave Crab)
  let _ = putStrLn (wave Fish)
  putStrLn (greet Crab)
